Reading: the gravitating field is suppressed far more than the particles at k 2-4 (the compensation removes core mass directly).
If shear traced the engine's gravitating field, F = 1 alone would sit about 3 sigma below both A_mod values in L100 and L50
(-3.0 to -3.4) and 1-2 sigma below in L25 (whose k = 1 bin is only 4 fundamental modes); adding any feedback band moves it to -2 .. -6 sigma;
this is post-hoc, z = 0.5 is scaled from z = 0, the boxes are not converged, and it is not a frozen verdict.
